namespace trion.propositional:
    primitive certificate, unchecked response, unconfirmed
    primitive adapter version, candidate, checked, checker version, conclusion
    primitive conversion, entailment witness, exhaustive result, incomplete, input provenance
    primitive interrupted search, malformed evidence, observed response, reconstructed outcome, replay
    primitive saved outcome, saved response, search, setting, unknown
    primitive unsatisfiable answer, value, witness, worker version

    source PROP-MMT-EVIDENCE:
        title "Propositional evidence in MMT proof results"
        locator "urn:trion:propositional:mmt-evidence:1"
        kind citation
        quote RULES """
The MMT proof verdict describes the asserted obligation.
The propositional result separately records the logical conclusion, premise status, execution, and evidence.
The certificate checker checks answers against the MMT formulas. The reference evaluator checks recovered valuations against the original Core.
When the full valuation scan fits its recorded budget, it must agree with each decided answer.
An unsatisfiable answer is unconfirmed when neither a complete reference scan nor a checked certificate verifies it. Incomplete enumeration alone establishes no exclusion.
An unsatisfiable premise set yields classical entailment and contradictory premises. The nonvacuous obligation is refuted.
An interrupted search can retain a checked witness. The absence of an answer supplies no proof of exclusion.
The report binds the fixed input, the question formulas, the answers, their scope, and verification settings to the obligation.
Replay rechecks those answers against the original MMT form and rejects changes to the subject, evidence, or result.
The outer verdict, reason, and question count of a propositional result agree with the reconstructed record. Its counterexample, when present, is the checked valuation of that record.
"""

    section "Applicability, execution, and logical conclusion":
        cite FOUNDATION
        The applicability of an adapter is applicable, unsupported, or precondition failed.
        The execution state of an analysis is not run, completed, undecided, timeout, resource limit, backend failure, or evidence rejected.
        The conclusion of an analysis is satisfiable, unsatisfiable, entailment, non-entailment, or absent conclusion.
        The premise status of an analysis is consistent, contradictory, unchecked, or undecided.
        The evidence of an analysis is checked model, checked counterexample, checked certificate, exhaustive, external response, or absent evidence.

        [R-UNVERIFIED]
        The propositional runner shall not report an unchecked response as a verified conclusion.
        The propositional checker shall not accept an unsat core as a certificate.

        [R-BINDING]
        If the evidence document differs from the query document, then the propositional checker shall reject the evidence.
        If the evidence query differs from the original query, then the propositional checker shall reject the evidence.
        If the evidence conversion differs from the original conversion, then the propositional checker shall reject the evidence.
        If the evidence settings differ from the original settings, then the propositional checker shall reject the evidence.
        The propositional checker shall reject evidence with a missing scope.
        The propositional checker shall reject malformed evidence.

        [R-WITNESS]
        The propositional checker shall require a value for every declaration slot.
        The propositional checker shall check a witness against the original premises.
        The propositional checker shall check an entailment witness against the negation of the original target.
        If the witness is checked and the search is incomplete, then the propositional checker shall accept the witness.

        [R-EXHAUSTIVE]
        The propositional checker shall report an exhaustive result only if the checker inspects every valuation.
        The propositional checker shall report entailment only if the checker checks the consistency of the premises.
        The propositional checker shall reject an unsatisfiable answer when a candidate exists.

        [R-NO-EXHAUSTION]
        If an unsatisfiable answer is unconfirmed, then the propositional checker shall report an external response.
            cite PROP-MMT-EVIDENCE#RULES
        If an unsatisfiable answer is unconfirmed, then the propositional checker shall leave the conclusion undecided.

        [R-FAILURE]
        The propositional runner shall report unknown as undecided.
        The propositional runner shall distinguish a timeout, a resource limit, and a backend failure.
        The propositional runner shall report a conclusion for an interrupted search only if the evidence is checked.

        [R-VACUITY]
        If contradictory premises entail a target, then the propositional runner shall report vacuous entailment.

        [R-CONFLICT]
        If checked results conflict, then the propositional runner shall preserve both records.
        If checked results conflict, then the propositional runner shall report an inconsistency.

    section "Reproducible analysis":
        cite FOUNDATION
        [R-SAVED]
        The propositional runner shall retain the document, query, and input provenance.
        The propositional runner shall retain the adapter version.
        The propositional runner shall retain the checker version.
        The propositional runner shall retain the worker version.
        The propositional runner shall retain the settings, resource limits, target problem, and observed response.

        [R-REPLAY]
        The propositional runner shall reconstruct the conversion during replay.
        The propositional runner shall check the saved response during replay.
        The propositional runner shall compare the reconstructed outcome to the saved outcome.

        [R-MMT-EVIDENCE]
        The propositional runner shall check the evidence of a propositional MMT result.
            cite PROP-MMT-EVIDENCE#RULES
